## THE THREE-TIER DEPLOYMENT DOCTRINE

| Tier | What it is | When to use | Cost | Hard Limit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Tier 1: Publish Artifact | One-click permanent public link from a Claude chat artifact | MVPs to validate demand | $0 | Compute billed to the end user, not you. Static HTML/JS artifacts are fully public — no viewer login. AI-powered artifacts (ones that call Claude's API at runtime) always require the viewer to be signed into Claude. |
| Tier 2: Static Hosting | GitHub Pages / Vercel / Netlify free tier | Custom domain, multi-page | $0 | No server-side logic |
| Tier 3: Real Backend | PythonAnywhere / Render free tier | Auth, cron, database | $0 on free tier | Full infrastructure to maintain |

**Rule:** Validate on Tier 1 first. Get 10 real users before touching Tier 2 or 3.

**The #1 beginner mistake:** doing more of the current tier (more polish, more features) instead of moving to the next one, or building Tier 3 infrastructure before Tier 1 has proven anyone wants the product.

