## PHASE 5A — PATH A: SINGLE HTML FILE (PRE-VALIDATION MVP)

### Artifact Build Rules
1. Describe the page's JOB, not its layout — the job defines success criteria, the layout is decoration
2. One core action per artifact — everything else is v2
3. Iterate 3–5 times max on one artifact before starting fresh — past that, diffs get messy and Claude starts contradicting earlier structure
4. Test on mobile explicitly — describe 375px-wide rendering before finalizing, since most traffic is mobile
5. Never ask for multi-page in one artifact — that needs Tier 2 hosting, not more prompting

**Copy-paste prompt:**
> "Build a single-file HTML landing page for [product]. Audience: [who]. One core action: [signup/buy/etc]. Explicitly test and describe how it will look on a 375px-wide mobile screen before finalizing."

### The Single-File Doctrine
One HTML file. No build step. No backend required for launch. Deployed in 30 seconds.

**Free Tier Stack**

| Layer | Tool | Free Tier Limit |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | HTML/CSS/JS (vanilla) | Unlimited |
| Deploy | Netlify Drop / Cloudflare Pages | Unlimited |
| Design | v0.dev | Free tier |
| AI Content | Claude Web Interface | Free tier |
| Images | Pollinations.ai | Free |
| Storage | `localStorage` (once deployed to Netlify/real hosting) — **if prototyping inside a Claude artifact instead, use `window.storage`; `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` are blocked in the artifact sandbox and fail silently** | 5–10MB |
| Payments (placeholder) | Stripe Payment Link | Free to create |

### The AI Build Loop
1. Write the complete spec as a Claude prompt (one message, complete requirements)
2. Paste output into a single `.html` file
3. Drag and drop to Netlify Drop
4. Send URL to first 10 potential customers — same day
5. Collect feedback before changing a single line of code

**Standard HTML MVP Template:**
```html
