## PHASE 5B — PATH B: FULL SAAS STACK (POST-VALIDATION)

**Do not build this until Phase 7 validation metrics are met.**

### Production Stack

| Layer | Tool | Free Tier |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | React + Vite + Tailwind | Free |
| Backend | Node.js + Express + tRPC | Free |
| Database | SQLite → Drizzle ORM | Free (local) |
| Auth | JWT (HttpOnly cookies) | Free (custom) |
| AI | Claude Sonnet API | ~$0.003/generation |
| Deploy | Render.com free tier | Free (750h/month) |
| Payments | Stripe Payment Link | Free (manual) |
| PDF Export | jsPDF (client-side) | Free |

**Scale Triggers (Migrate when these hit):**
- SQLite file >500MB → Postgres (Supabase)
- >10K concurrent users → Vercel + Edge functions
- 10+ paying clients → Add Stripe webhooks
- >$5K MRR → Next.js + Vercel + full webhook automation

### MCP + Automation Pipelines
- MCP (Model Context Protocol) lets an AI-powered artifact or Claude session call external tools directly — Google Drive, Gmail, Slack, or a custom server
- Limitation: requires the viewer to be logged into Claude — can't be made fully public/no-login
- One integration shipped beats three half-built — pick the single manual step users hate most
- Classify recurring tasks: mechanical (no judgment needed) → automate. Requires a human decision → keep interactive, but pre-fill everything possible
- Automate only after 5+ correct manual runs — you can't automate a process you don't understand yet
- Log every automated run somewhere checkable — silent automation that fails silently is worse than doing it manually

### Core Database Schema (Drizzle + SQLite)

```typescript
// drizzle/schema.ts
import { sqliteTable, text, integer } from "drizzle-orm/sqlite-core";
import { sql } from "drizzle-orm";

export const users = sqliteTable("users", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey().$defaultFn(() => crypto.randomUUID()),
  email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
  passwordHash: text("password_hash").notNull(),
  plan: text("plan", { enum: ["trial", "pro"] }).default("trial").notNull(),
  trialItemsUsed: integer("trial_items_used").default(0).notNull(),
  createdAt: text("created_at").default(sql`(datetime('now'))`).notNull(),
  updatedAt: text("updated_at").default(sql`(datetime('now'))`).notNull(),
});
```

### AI Integration Pattern

**Core Rule: Always request JSON output. Always parse with a regex fallback.**

```typescript
export async function generateOutput(input: YourInput): Promise<YourOutput> {
  const response = await client.messages.create({
    model: "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
    max_tokens: 1024,
    system: SYSTEM_PROMPT,
    messages: [{ role: "user", content: buildUserPrompt(input) }],
  });

  const text = response.content[0].type === "text" ? response.content[0].text : "";
  const jsonMatch = text.match(/\{[\s\S]*\}/);
  if (!jsonMatch) throw new Error("Could not parse AI response");
  return JSON.parse(jsonMatch[0]) as YourOutput;
}
```

**System Prompt Structure:**
```
You are a [role with 20+ years experience] specializing in [specific output type].
You [quality standard — never use clichés].
You [emotional/professional outcome].

Respond ONLY with valid JSON in this exact format:
{
  "headline": "string",
  "body": "string",
  "highlights": ["string", "string"],
  "closingLine": "string"
}
```

**AI cost:** Claude Sonnet at ~1K input + 500 output = ~$0.003/generation. At any viable price point ($49+/month), AI cost is operationally zero.

