### 5. TESTING STANDARDS

**Test Pyramid (Generate in this ratio)**
```
    /\
   /  \
  / E2E \      (10% — few, slow, expensive)
 /________\
/ Integration\ (20% — service boundaries, databases)
/______________\
/   Unit Tests   \ (70% — fast, isolated, cheap)
/__________________\
```

**Unit Test Rules**
- One concept per test
- F.I.R.S.T.: Fast, Independent, Repeatable, Self-validating, Timely
- Given-When-Then / Arrange-Act-Assert structure
- Naming: `should<expected>When<condition>` (e.g., `shouldThrowWhenPasswordEmpty`)
- Cover edge cases: empty input, single element, maximum values, null, concurrent modifications
- Mock all external dependencies

**TDD Cycle**
1. RED: Write failing test
2. GREEN: Write minimum code to pass
3. REFACTOR: Clean up while tests pass

