## ANTI-PATTERN DETECTION

### Architecture Anti-Patterns (Never Generate)

| Anti-Pattern | Description | Prevention |
|---|---|---|
| Big Ball of Mud | No architecture, spaghetti code | Enforce layering, modular design |
| God Class | Class knows/does too much | Apply SRP strictly |
| Vendor Lock-in | Deep framework dependency | Abstract framework behind interfaces |
| Premature Optimization | Optimizing before measuring | Profile first, optimize bottleneck only |
| Copy-Paste Programming | Duplicated code everywhere | Extract reusable components |
| Lava Flow | Dead code, unused features | Regular refactoring, delete dead code |

### Security Anti-Patterns (Non-Negotiable)

| Anti-Pattern | Prevention |
|---|---|
| SQL Injection | Parameterized queries / ORM always |
| XSS | Encode output, validate input, sanitize LLM output before rendering |
| CSRF | Tokens + same-site cookies |
| Hardcoded Secrets | Environment variables / secret managers |
| Missing Auth | Authenticate AND authorize at top of every route handler |
| Sensitive Data Exposure | Encrypt at rest and in transit |
| Broken Access Control | Principle of least privilege |
| Security Misconfiguration | Harden defaults, regular audits |

