## PHASE 6 — DISTRIBUTION & LAUNCH

**Distribution is the product. A great app no one finds is a hobby.**

### 6.1 Channel Priority (Order by Conversion Rate)

| Channel | Best For | Trust Level |
|---|---|---|
| WhatsApp DMs to known contacts | B2B local, highest conversion | Highest |
| Instagram DMs to local professionals | Warm outreach, visual proof | High |
| Facebook Groups for the niche | Community presence, medium intent | Medium |
| LinkedIn text posts | B2B, professional pain | Medium (slow) |
| TikTok organic | B2C, visual products, viral potential | Variable |
| Reddit communities (r/niche) | Anonymous pain, high intent | Medium |
| SEO long-form | Search-intent, educational products | Low (slow) |

**For Trinidad & Tobago:** WhatsApp → Instagram → Facebook Groups → LinkedIn → TikTok

### 6.1b Content-as-Distribution Engine
- Every post ends with: "I built this in an afternoon with Claude — try it: [link]"
- Build process IS content: "How I built X in 20 minutes" = proof + marketing in one piece
- Track which specific piece of content drove which specific signup — without this you're guessing
- Never separate "content business" from "tools business": each tool is proof for the content, each piece of content is the funnel for the tool. Separate them and both starve.

### 6.2 The DM Template (Copy-Paste Ready)

```
Hey [Name],

I noticed you do [their specific task] — I built a tool that [does that task]
in [time] instead of [current time]. It's in free trial right now — no card needed.

Want to try it with your next [specific work item]?
```

**Target conversion:** 10 DMs → 2 demos → 1 sale. If worse: the problem or demo is wrong, not the tool.

### 6.3 TikTok Content System (B2C / Viral Products)

**Format Hierarchy (by conversion rate):**
1. Screen recording + founder voiceover
2. Text post — zero filming, pure story
3. Stitch/Duet — piggyback on viral niche content
4. Carousel — before/during/after sequence
5. Talking head — only when face is a genuine conversion asset

**7-Day Launch Calendar:**

| Day | Format | Hook | CTA |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Origin story | "I was $[exact amount] in [specific situation]" | "Link in bio" |
| 2 | Screen demo | "POV: You have [problem]. This solves it in 30 seconds." | "Try it free" |
| 3 | Social proof | "I showed [person] this. They [specific reaction]." | "Tag someone" |
| 4 | Streak/milestone | "Day X of [action]. [Number] achieved." | "Start yours" |
| 5 | Victory moment | "I just [achieved thing]. Here's the proof." | "Your turn" |
| 6 | Comparison | "[Old way] vs [my way] — which would you choose?" | "Comment below" |
| 7 | Community | Stitch with popular niche video | "Link in bio" |

**Engagement Protocol (First 2 Hours After Post):**
- Reply to every comment with a question back
- Pin one comment that drives profile visits
- 30 min/day: Comment genuinely on 20 posts in niche hashtags

### 6.3b Pricing & Monetization Mechanics
- MRR compounds, one-time doesn't — at zero-budget-founder numbers, recurring revenue is survival, not preference
- Start with a single price point, not three tiers — tiers are a segmentation optimization for when you have 20+ paying users, not zero
- Price to the outcome, not build time — a 20-minute build that saves someone 10 hours is worth more than a 2-month build that saves 10 minutes
- Don't underprice out of guilt — you can discount later, you can't easily raise price on existing users

### 6.4 Specificity Is the Trump Card

"$242,855.83 in debt" builds more belief than any face. Exact numbers are the hook. Never round them.

### 6.5 Week 1 Success Metrics

| Metric | Target | Action if Missed |
|---|---|---|
| DMs sent | 50+ | Send more — volume beats optimization at zero traction |
| Demo conversations | 5+ | Hook isn't working. Change one element, not everything. |
| App users (free trial) | 20–50 | Product promise unclear. Add a demo video. |
| "How do I pay?" questions | 3+ | Value isn't visible fast enough. Cut steps to first output. |
| First paying customer | 1 | Pricing friction. Try $99 lifetime deal first. |

